# Component documentation

Every component page in `docs/components/` (excluding `overview.md`) must follow this contract.

## Required sections (in order)

> **Machine-readable version:** `tooling/lib/markdown-sections.json` contains this section list as structured data — heading name, index, required flag, conditional rules, and per-section notes. Scripts and agents must import the JSON instead of hardcoding the list.

Only these H2 headings are allowed in component pages, in this exact canonical order:

1. `## Overview`
2. `## Anatomy`
3. `## Component API`
4. `## Visual Specifications`
5. `## Variants`
6. `## States`
7. `## Usage Guidelines`
8. `## Content Guidelines`
9. `## Accessibility`
10. `## Related Components`
11. `## Design–Token Discrepancies` (optional, only when real mismatches exist)
12. `## Gaps / TBD` (optional, deterministic binary contract)

No other H2 headings are permitted (`## Examples`, `## Changelog`, etc.).
If additional details are needed, place them under `###` inside the nearest allowed H2.

## `## Gaps / TBD` deterministic contract

> **Machine-readable specification:** `tooling/scripts/lib/gaps-contract.mjs` (canonical contract and validation rules) and `tooling/scripts/lib/gaps.mjs` (gap detection logic). For code semantics and blocking policy (`GAP00`–`GAP02`), see `error-codes.mdc` and `.agents/rules/_manifest.yml` (`checks`).

- This section is **binary and deterministic**:
  - Include it when unresolved gaps exist in the linked spec.
  - Omit it entirely when no unresolved gaps exist.
- Each item must use checkbox format:
  - `- [ ] [SCHEMA_TBD] ...`
  - `- [ ] [TOKEN_INVALID] ...`
  - `- [ ] [CONTENT_UNKNOWN] ...`
  - `- [ ] [A11Y_TBD] ...`
- Canonical ordering is mandatory:
  1. `SCHEMA_TBD`
  2. `TOKEN_INVALID`
  3. `CONTENT_UNKNOWN`
  4. `A11Y_TBD`
- When gaps exist and the page lifecycle state is `ready`, emit **`GAP02`** (see `error-codes.mdc`); resolve all gaps first.

## General rules

- Every required section (1–10) must be present; when data is missing, use `TBD` instead of omitting sections.
- Do not add H2 headings outside the canonical allowed list.
- One component per file. File name matches component name in `snake_case` (for example, `status_bar.md`).

## Writing style

- Keep prose concise and scannable.
- Prefer bullets and tables over long paragraphs.
- Use factual statements only; unknown values must be `TBD`.
- Keep language and tone aligned with `docs-language-tone.mdc`.

## Section guidance

### `# {ComponentName}`

- Immediately after the H1, include one single-line description.

### `## Overview`

- Explain component purpose and role.
- Include Figma component/set name and core variant properties.
- Include a `### Visual Proof` subsection with:
  - a screenshot link captured from Figma (`figma_take_screenshot` workflow),
  - source node id,
  - generated proof artifact path.
- For `draft` / `needs-review`, use explicit `TBD` placeholders when capture is not yet available.

### `## Anatomy`

- Use a numbered list with bold part names.
- Each item explains role (container, label, icon, etc.).

### `## Component API`

- Include `### Properties` with table schema:
  `| Name | Type | Default | Required | Description |`
- Convert spec `type` values to Figma display types using `tooling/lib/property-type-map.json` (canonical machine-readable mapping). Do not duplicate the mapping here.
- Spec types are canonical **lowercase** (e.g. `enum`, `boolean`); Figma display types are **uppercase** (e.g. `VARIANT`, `BOOLEAN`).

### `## Visual Specifications`

- Organize by subareas (container, typography, spacing, iconography as applicable).
- Pair token references with concrete fallback values.

### `## Variants`

- Prefer a table when differences are token-driven and repetitive.
- Include variant name, token(s), fallback(s), and short note.

### `## States`

- Cover applicable states (`default`, `hover`, `focus`, `pressed/active`, `disabled`, `loading`).
- For non-interactive components, explicitly state no interactive states.

### `## Usage Guidelines`

- Include when-to-use and when-not-to-use guidance.
- Include actionable do/don't bullets.
- Include a `### Behavior` subsection that captures:
  - interaction notes,
  - responsive behavior,
  - overflow/truncation behavior,
  - i18n/RTL implications when applicable.
- Include a `### Examples` subsection with at least:
  - one basic usage example,
  - one contextual/real-world usage example.
- If behavior or examples are not yet verified, use explicit `TBD` placeholders and track them in `## Gaps / TBD`.

### `## Content Guidelines`

- Define component-specific writing guidance (tone, casing, length constraints, punctuation).
- If no user-facing text exists, state that explicitly.

### `## Accessibility`

- Cover role, keyboard interaction, focus management, labeling, and contrast.
- Follow `inclusive-docs.mdc` for detailed accessibility and i18n guidance.

### `## Related Components`

- Link sibling/alternative components with one-line differentiation.
- If a changelog is needed, use `### Changelog` inside this section.

### `## Design–Token Discrepancies` (optional)

- Include only with verifiable mismatches.
- Follow `design-token-discrepancies.mdc`.
